# DSA_TASK_012 — PRE-COMPUTED SETUP CANDIDATES MODULE v1.3.0-alpha1 (2026-09-04) — Formal Spec for Java Developer (DSA Team/JISHU) — Status: APPROVED — Scope: Move all deterministic math + proof detection from Python/AI to Java/DSA. Emit one `setup_candidates` array per snapshot. AI validates top candidate only. — Time Estimate: ~14 hours (Phase 1: 6h math/state, Phase 2: 8h proof detection) — Backward Compatibility: DSA emits BOTH old flat fields + new `setup_candidates`. Legacy `math_object_builder.py` still works on old JSON. No breaking changes. — Schema Version: v1.2.0 → v1.3.0 (additive only) — --- ## 1. TOP-LEVEL JSON ADDITION Add ONE new top-level field to the existing DSA snapshot JSON: ```json { // ... all existing v1.2.0 fields unchanged ... // NEW: setup_candidates array (may be empty) setup_candidates: [ { rank: 1, setup_type: ct_short, direction: short, zone: { name: pf_vah, price: 78748.88, type: pf_vah }, math: { distance_pct: 0.51, distance_cap: 0.4, tier: trigger_ready, substate: above, stop: 78774.0, target: 77977.15, gross_rr: 5.34, net_rr: 4.01, rr_sanity: true }, proof: { rejection_wick: STRONG, absorption: { detected: true, strength: moderate }, finished_auction: { detected: false }, delta_flip: { detected: true, from_negative: true }, volume_spike: { detected: false }, speed: { picking_up: false }, cvd_aligned: false, book_imbalance: 0.63 }, score: { raw: 72, confidence: B, proof_count: 3, confluence_bonus: 10 } } ] } ``` If no valid setup exists, emit: `setup_candidates: []` --- ## 2. ALGORITHM: HOW DSA BUILDS setup_candidates (Java Implementation Guide) ### STEP 1: STATE CLASSIFICATION (from existing fields) Input: `daily_vp.shape`, `weekly_vp.shape`, `vwap.slope`, `cvd.slope`, `conditions.price_vs_va`, `conditions.price_vs_poc`, `weekly_vp.prior_week_poc`, `weekly_vp.two_week_ago_poc` Output: `state` enum: `balance` | `trend_healthy` | `trend_unhealthy` | `transition` Algorithm (deterministic): 1. Primary signal: `daily_vp.shape` — B → balance, P/D → trend 2. Secondary: `weekly_vp.shape` — weekly B overrides daily P/D to balance 3. VWAP slope: `sideways` → balance, `sloped`/`steep` → trend 4. CVD: `flat` + price oscillating → balance; `aligned` → trend; `divergent` → trend_unhealthy 5. Price vs VWAP: oscillating → balance; one side → trend; extended → trend_unhealthy 6. VPOC migration: rising/falling sequence → trend_healthy; choppy → transition 7. Higher TF wins: weekly > daily > intraday --- ### STEP 2: DIRECTIONAL FILTER (from existing fields) Input: `conditions.price_vs_va`, `conditions.price_vs_poc` Output: `evaluated_directions` array: [`short`, `long`, `both`] Algorithm: 1. If `price_vs_va` = above_va → evaluate UPPER zones for SHORTS only 2. If `price_vs_va` = below_va → evaluate LOWER zones for LONGS only 3. If `price_vs_va` = in_va → evaluate BOTH VAH and VAL 4. If `price_vs_va` = in_va AND `price_vs_poc` = above → bias toward upper zones 5. If `price_vs_va` = in_va AND `price_vs_poc` = below → bias toward lower zones --- ### STEP 3: ZONE EXTRACTION (from existing fields) Extract all zone prices into internal list (same as `math_object_builder.py` `_extract_zones()`): | Zone Source | Name Prefix | Type | |-------------|-------------|------| | weekly_vp.poc/vah/val | weekly_poc, weekly_vah, weekly_val | weekly_poc, weekly_vah, weekly_val | | daily_vp.poc/vah/val | daily_poc, daily_vah, daily_val | daily_poc, daily_vah, daily_val | | post_funding_vp.poc/vah/val | pf_poc, pf_vah, pf_val | pf_poc, pf_vah, pf_val | | intraday_4h_vp.poc/vah/val | 4h_poc, 4h_vah, 4h_val | 4h_poc, 4h_vah, 4h_val | | vwap.price | vwap | vwap_band | | vwap.bands.* | vwap_band_+1, vwap_band_+2, etc. | vwap_band | | prior_day.poc/vah/val/close | prior_day_poc, prior_day_vah, prior_day_val, prior_day_close | prior_day_poc, prior_day_vah, prior_day_val, prior_day_close | | structure.1h.swing_high/low | 1h_swing_high, 1h_swing_low | swing_high_1h, swing_low_1h | | structure.15m.swing_high/low | 15m_swing_high, 15m_swing_low | swing_high_15m, swing_low_15m | | structure.5m.swing_high/low | 5m_swing_high, 5m_swing_low | swing_high_5m, swing_low_5m | | conditions.fvg_nearest_unfilled | fvg_nearest | fvg | | naked_poc.naked_pocs[] | naked_poc_YYYY-MM-DD | weekly_poc | --- ### STEP 4: DISTANCE + CAP + TIER (per zone) For each zone: 1. `distance_pct = abs(price - zone_price) / price * 100` 2. `cap = get_distance_cap(zone_type, speed_picking_up)` — use existing caps from `mts_math.py`: | Zone Type | Cap | |-----------|-----| | weekly_poc/vah/val | 0.5% | | daily_poc/vah/val | 0.4% | | 4h_poc/vah/val, pf_poc/vah/val | 0.4% | | prior_day_poc/vah/val/close | 0.4% | | swing_high_1h, swing_low_1h | 0.5% | | swing_high_15m, swing_low_15m | 0.3% | | swing_high_5m, swing_low_5m | 0.3% | | vwap_band | 0.2% | | fvg | 0.2% | 3. If `speed_picking_up = true`: caps remain unchanged (contextual adjustment only, per engine Sec 2.6) 4. Tier assignment: | Distance | Tier | |----------|------| | 0.0% – 0.1% | trigger_ready | | 0.1% – cap | conditional | | > cap | ignore | 5. If tier = ignore → skip zone (do not include in candidates) --- ### STEP 5: SETUP TYPE ASSIGNMENT (per zone + direction) For each zone that passes tier filter, assign valid setup types based on zone type + directional filter: | Zone | Short Setup | Long Setup | |------|-------------|------------| | VAH (weekly/daily/4h/pf) | CT Short | — | | VAL (weekly/daily/4h/pf) | — | CT Long | | POC | CT (unhealthy trend only) | CT (unhealthy trend only) | | VWAP band | Scalp (if sideways) | Scalp (if sideways) | | FVG | EXIT only | EXIT only | | Swing High | CT Short (with confluence) | — | | Swing Low | — | CT Long (with confluence) | | Prior Day VAH | CT Short | — | | Prior Day VAL | — | CT Long | | Prior Day POC | CT (unhealthy) | CT (unhealthy) | | Prior Day Close | CT Short (if above) | CT Long (if below) | Filter by state: - `balance` → CT priority, Scalp if sideways - `trend_healthy` → TC/BO priority, CT at extremes only - `trend_unhealthy` → CT possible, requires exhaustion proof - `transition` → WAIT (no setups) --- ### STEP 6: STOP + TARGET SELECTION (per setup candidate) For each valid (zone, setup_type) pair: 1. Determine swing TF for stop: | Zone Type | Swing TF | |-----------|----------| | weekly_* | 1h | | daily_*, 4h_*, pf_*, prior_day_* | 15m | | vwap_*, fvg_*, swing_*_5m | 5m | | swing_*_15m | 15m | | swing_*_1h | 1h | 2. Stop selection: - Short setup: `stop = structure.{swing_tf}.swing_high` (must be > zone_price) - Long setup: `stop = structure.{swing_tf}.swing_low` (must be < zone_price) 3. Target selection: - Collect all POCs: weekly, daily, post_funding, intraday_4h, prior_day - Short target: nearest POC < zone_price (max of candidates) - Long target: nearest POC > zone_price (min of candidates) - Add VWAP price as candidate if in trade direction 4. If stop or target is null → discard candidate --- ### STEP 7: R:R CALCULATION (per candidate) If stop and target both exist: 1. `gross_rr = abs(target - zone_price) / abs(zone_price - stop)` 2. `net_rr = gross_rr * 0.75` (25% friction haircut) 3. `rr_sanity = gross_rr >= 1.5` 4. If `rr_sanity = false` → discard candidate --- ### STEP 8: CONFLUENCE DETECTION Group all remaining candidate zones. Two zones are in confluence if their prices are within 0.3% of EACH OTHER (not just price). For each candidate, if it belongs to a confluence cluster of 2+ zones: - `confluence_bonus = 10` (contextual weight, not numeric score modifier) --- ### STEP 9: PROOF DETECTION (Phase 2 — requires bar-level data) DSA must have access to recent 1m or 5m bar data (OHLC + volume + delta) to compute these. If bar data unavailable, emit `detected: false` for all proof fields. #### 9.1 rejection_wick (enum: NONE / WEAK / MODERATE / STRONG) For each of last 20 bars at zone level: 1. Check if wick touches zone: - Support rejection: `wick_low <= zone AND close > zone` - Resistance rejection: `wick_high >= zone AND close < zone` 2. If touched: `body_pct = abs(close - open) / (high - low)` `wick_pct = 1.0 - body_pct` 3. Quality: | wick_pct | body_pct | Quality | |----------|----------|---------| | > 0.8 | < 0.2 | STRONG | | > 0.5 | < 0.5 | MODERATE | | any | any | WEAK | Return highest quality found across all bars. If none touched → NONE. #### 9.2 absorption (object: {detected, strength, candle_count, vol_ratio}) For each of last 10 bars where price within 0.1% of zone: 1. `volume > 2.0 * avg_volume_20` 2. `(high - low) < 0.3 * atr_14` 3. Delta opposite to price direction: - `delta > 0 AND close < open` (buying pressure but price down) - `delta < 0 AND close > open` (selling pressure but price up) If 1+2+3 true for any bar: - `detected = true` - `strength = (max_vol / avg_vol > 5.0) ? strong : moderate` - `candle_count = count of matching bars` - `vol_ratio = max_vol / avg_vol` #### 9.3 finished_auction (object: {detected, direction, extreme_delta, reversal_delta, follow_through}) For each bar i in last 20: 1. `abs(bar[i].delta) > 3.0 * avg_delta_20` → extreme delta 2. Next bar reverses: - `bar[i].delta < 0 AND bar[i+1].close > bar[i].close` (sell extreme → reversal up) - `bar[i].delta > 0 AND bar[i+1].close < bar[i].close` (buy extreme → reversal down) 3. No follow-through: `abs(bar[i+1].delta) < 0.5 * abs(bar[i].delta)` If all 3: - `detected = true` - `direction = bar[i].delta < 0 ? sell : buy` - `extreme_delta = bar[i].delta` - `reversal_delta = bar[i+1].delta` - `follow_through = false` #### 9.4 delta_flip (object: {detected, from_negative, at_zone, zone_level, candles_since}) For each bar i in last 20: 1. `bar[i-1].delta < 0 AND bar[i].delta > 0` (negative → positive) OR `bar[i-1].delta > 0 AND bar[i].delta < 0` (positive → negative) 2. `abs(bar[i].close - zone_level) < 0.001 * zone_level` (within 0.1% of zone) If both: - `detected = true` - `from_negative = bar[i-1].delta < 0` - `at_zone = true` - `zone_level = zone_level` - `candles_since = bars.length - i` #### 9.5 volume_spike (object: {detected, magnitude, at_level, level}) Refactor existing `volume_spike_at_level` boolean: 1. `magnitude = current_volume / avg_volume_4h` 2. `detected = magnitude > 2.0` 3. `at_level = price within 0.1% of zone` 4. `level = zone_price` #### 9.6 speed (object: {picking_up, score, direction, atr_ratio, consecutive_large}) Refactor existing `speed_picking_up` boolean: 1. `atr_current = atr_14` 2. `atr_baseline = atr_14 over prior 20 bars` 3. `atr_ratio = atr_current / atr_baseline` 4. `large_candles = count of last 10 bars where (high-low) > 1.5 * avg_range` 5. `consecutive = max consecutive large candles` 6. `score = min(10, (atr_ratio * 3) + (consecutive * 2))` 7. `picking_up = score > 5` 8. `direction = price_trend_direction` #### 9.7 cvd_aligned (boolean) `cvd.slope` direction matches `trade_flow.net_delta` direction: - CVD rising + net_delta > 0 → true - CVD falling + net_delta < 0 → true - Otherwise → false Use `cvd_recent.slope_1h` as tiebreaker if main CVD slope ambiguous. --- ### STEP 10: SCORING (per candidate) `raw_score` is a composite for ranking only. NOT a verdict. AI still judges contextually. ```java int proof_count = 0; if (!rejection_wick.equals(NONE)) proof_count++; if (absorption.detected) proof_count++; if (finished_auction.detected) proof_count++; if (delta_flip.detected) proof_count++; if (volume_spike.detected) proof_count++; if (speed.picking_up) proof_count++; if (cvd_aligned) proof_count++; if (book_imbalance < 0.4 || book_imbalance > 0.6) proof_count++; // imbalance = directional signal int raw = 50; // base raw += proof_count * 7; // +7 per proof signal raw += confluence_bonus; // +10 if in confluence cluster // Cap at 95 raw = Math.min(95, raw); // Confidence band String confidence; if (raw >= 70) confidence = B; else if (raw >= 55) confidence = C+; else if (raw >= 40) confidence = C; else confidence = D; ``` --- ### STEP 11: RANKING + OUTPUT 1. Sort all candidates by `raw_score` descending 2. If tie, prefer: higher TF zone > lower TF zone 3. Assign `rank` 1, 2, 3... 4. Emit top N candidates (recommend N=3 max to keep JSON compact) 5. If no candidates pass all filters → emit `[]` --- ## 3. BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY DSA emits BOTH during transition (minimum 2 weeks): ```json { // OLD fields (v1.2.0) — still present rejection_wick_at_zone: true, volume_spike_at_level: true, speed_picking_up: false, // NEW fields (v1.3.0) setup_candidates: [ { proof: { rejection_wick: STRONG, volume_spike: { detected: true, magnitude: 3.5 }, speed: { picking_up: false, score: 3 } } } ] } ``` Legacy `math_object_builder.py` reads old fields. New code reads `setup_candidates`. Both work. After transition (Week 3+), old booleans may be deprecated. --- ## 4. VALIDATION PROTOCOL (Rule 32) After Phase 1+2 implementation, test on 3 historical snapshots: | Test | Check | Pass Criteria | |------|-------|-------------| | 1 | DSA rank 1 candidate == AI manually computed rank 1 | Match on zone + setup_type | | 2 | DSA proof signals match screenshot visual analysis | 2+ of 3 snapshots agree | | 3 | DSA state classification matches AI state | 3/3 match | | 4 | DSA R:R matches Python `math_object_builder` | Within 0.01 tolerance | If any test fails → debug DSA algorithm before integration. --- ## 5. ENGINE INTEGRATION (After DSA Validation) 1. `math_object_builder.py` updated to read `setup_candidates` directly (skip zone extraction + math) 2. AI judgment layer receives `setup_candidates[0]` as primary candidate 3. AI validates: cross-check proof signals, apply session context, apply hard stops 4. AI generates verdict + card 5. Screenshot becomes OPTIONAL quality check, not requirement --- ## 6. CROSS-TRADER GAP UNLOCKS | This Field | Unlocks Entry | Engine Section | |------------|--------------|----------------| | proof.absorption | C03-E01 (Heavy Selling + No Breakdown = Absorption) | Sec 4 Proof Types | | zone_intelligence.test_count | C06-E01 (Test Count Degradation) | Sec 2.7 Confluence | | proof.finished_auction | Tom footprint proof | Sec 4 Proof Types | | proof.delta_flip | Tom CVD proof | Sec 4 Proof Types | --- ## 7. WHAT'S EXCLUDED (Not in This Task) | Item | Why Excluded | |------|-------------| | Liquidation data fix | DSA infrastructure issue, not a field spec | | Trade flow timeframe tag | Metadata, not proof | | Zone test count | Requires 48h history — may not be available | | CVD divergence expansion | Boolean works; expansion is polish | | Composite profiles | VP histogram API limitation | | Fibonacci retracements | Not a Tom concept | --- # END